Subject: [PATCH v6 0/3] dm zoned: fix idle reclaim problems

Mikulas,

v4 of this series is already in dm-7.4 (acce1b6ac, 60427628f,
ac82aa060); I missed that when I sent v5, sorry for the noise. v6 folds
the new patch 4 of v5 into patch 1, as Damien asked. Patches 2 and 3
have the same code as in dm-7.4. If you would rather keep dm-7.4 as it
is, the difference can go on top of it as a single patch; I can send
that, with the commit message of patch 1 here, instead. Please tell me
which you prefer.

What is new compared with v4 (now in patch 1): an idle target whose
random (and cache) zones are all free never stops running its reclaim
work. Since 90a9b8693f1b ("dm zoned: reclaim random zones when idle"),
dmz_should_reclaim() treats "idle" plus a non-zero total number of
random zones as "reclaim now", dmz_do_reclaim() finds no candidate and
returns -EBUSY, dmz_check_dev() checks every device for media events (a
TEST UNIT READY on SCSI disks), and the work is requeued with no delay.
In mainline the loop can end when a pass finishes while the target is
busy with enough free zones; with patch 3 the idle poll stays armed, so
the loop recurs whenever the target becomes idle.

Measured on 7.3-rc7 with three emulated host-managed members of an md
RAID5, the target idle, SCSI commands to the members over 30 s:

  stock dm-zoned   5,804,292 commands (193,476/s)   30 % kernel CPU
  v6                      18 commands                0 % kernel CPU

v4 (in dm-7.4) behaves like stock here: 187,707 commands/s and 31 %
kernel CPU in an earlier run. With v6 the random zones filled by a
2 GiB write burst were free again 90 seconds after the target became
idle. On three 27 TB host-managed SATA drives (7.2.10 with an earlier
version of the series) the loop kept about three CPUs busy with about
155,000 TEST UNIT READY commands per second issued to each drive's SCSI
device; libata completes those without sending anything to the drive,
so the cost was CPU time. With the fix, under one command per second
per drive.

Changes since v5:
 - patch 4 folded into patch 1 (Damien), which is now titled "dm zoned:
   back off when reclaim cannot make progress"; its Reviewed-by tags
   are dropped because the patch changed
 - patch 1: the comment and the commit message no longer say that no
   I/O failed (-ENOSPC can also come from a failed metadata write)
 - patch 3: commit message mentions -EBUSY next to -ENOSPC (no code
   change)
 - commit message: TEST UNIT READY on SATA drives is completed by
   libata, the cost of the loop was CPU time

illofspeed (3):
  dm zoned: back off when reclaim cannot make progress
  dm zoned: do not reclaim a random zone into another random zone
  dm zoned: keep polling for idle reclaim after a reclaim pass

